          </summary>
          <p class="text-slate-500 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-3 pl-10">A spreadsheet holds what someone typed. SiteGov holds what&rsquo;s actually running. It finds the DNS provider your spreadsheet doesn&rsquo;t list, the SSL cert expiring in 11 days, and the nameserver that changed last Tuesday. The spreadsheet is a good intention. SiteGov is a live record.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="faq py-6">
